WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.244 --> 00:00:02.632
- [Man] The word non-profit
scares me a little bit

00:00:02.632 --> 00:00:04.519
but it freaks the hell 
out of my parents.

00:00:04.519 --> 00:00:06.524
Have you ever wanted to 
do something that you knew

00:00:06.524 --> 00:00:08.318
there was little to no money in

00:00:08.318 --> 00:00:10.159
and can you offer 
myself any advice?

00:00:10.159 --> 00:00:12.574
- Yes. No, I've never 
wanted to do that.

00:00:12.574 --> 00:00:15.451
(laughter)

00:00:15.451 --> 00:00:18.007
You can keep the mic 
for a second but

00:00:18.007 --> 00:00:20.183
it's really interesting timing
that you ask this.

00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:23.034
I'm on the board of a 
non-profit called

00:00:23.034 --> 00:00:24.983
Pencils of Promise.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:29.369
And POP was started by an 
unbelievable young man

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:31.411
named Adam Braun.

00:00:31.411 --> 00:00:34.601
Adam Braun's brother 
happens to be Scooter Braun

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.983
the guy who discovered
Justin Bieber.

00:00:36.983 --> 00:00:39.118
Here are two brothers
and they went in very,

00:00:39.118 --> 00:00:40.337
very different directions.

00:00:40.337 --> 00:00:43.561
Now imagine your bro
who's a year younger or

00:00:43.561 --> 00:00:45.254
older, excuse me, 
in this scenario

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:47.448
not only didn't go non-profit

00:00:47.448 --> 00:00:50.695
but went and fucking 
found the Biebs.

00:00:50.695 --> 00:00:51.530
Right?

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.920
And made tens of 
millions of dollars.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.186
He's run POP for about 
a decade and now

00:00:56.186 --> 00:00:58.565
he just got married a 
couple years ago

00:00:58.565 --> 00:01:01.010
and not making any money
has gotten to a place in

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.088
his life where he's already 
done more good for the world

00:01:04.088 --> 00:01:08.124
than 99% of people and
he's now going, he's just left

00:01:08.124 --> 00:01:09.600
and he's now our 
Chairman Emeritus

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.048
but he's no longer involved.

00:01:11.048 --> 00:01:12.265
And he's going and 
trying to build

00:01:12.265 --> 00:01:14.397
what he now needs financially.

00:01:14.397 --> 00:01:16.611
I'll tell you this,
we've never lived through

00:01:16.611 --> 00:01:19.685
a generation where young people
are willing to go that path.

00:01:19.685 --> 00:01:21.754
The cliché path is the way
I always thought about the way

00:01:21.754 --> 00:01:23.193
I was going to give back.

00:01:23.193 --> 00:01:25.414
Right? Build a huge empire.

00:01:25.414 --> 00:01:28.855
Buy the Jets and then 
start giving back. Right?

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:32.144
I got affected five to seven 
years ago by Scott Harrison

00:01:32.144 --> 00:01:34.087
who's the founder 
of Charity: Water.

00:01:34.087 --> 00:01:36.155
Also very 
progressive non-profit.

00:01:36.155 --> 00:01:38.578
And he said, "Gary, you 
can give along the way.

00:01:38.578 --> 00:01:40.397
"You don't have to build 
it all up and give it away."

00:01:40.397 --> 00:01:41.246
And I've done that.

00:01:41.246 --> 00:01:43.344
And it's been very 
rewarding to me but

00:01:43.344 --> 00:01:44.349
as a lot of you know,

00:01:44.349 --> 00:01:46.513
I don't talk a lot about 
my non-profit work.

00:01:46.513 --> 00:01:48.826
I think, there's a lot of things
I keep private.

00:01:48.826 --> 00:01:50.611
My kids. You know, it's funny,

00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:52.461
I keep all my good shit private,

00:01:52.461 --> 00:01:54.752
you know, I just do. 
It's just how I roll

00:01:54.752 --> 00:01:58.017
but I don't think anybody can 
tell you how to live your life.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:01.825
You just need to make sure
that you mean it.

00:02:01.825 --> 00:02:04.730
So I have a lot of 23, 
24-year-olds,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.714
22-year-olds right now 
that don't know exactly

00:02:06.714 --> 00:02:09.220
what they want to do and 
they've painted a narrative

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.356
that they want to be 
a non-profit because

00:02:11.356 --> 00:02:14.737
they like the brand association
of making themselves feel

00:02:14.737 --> 00:02:16.793
like they're better human beings
than the other people.

00:02:16.793 --> 00:02:18.279
I'm not joking.

00:02:18.279 --> 00:02:20.505
You need to make sure 
is that what you're doing or

00:02:20.505 --> 00:02:21.756
do you actually want to do it?

00:02:21.756 --> 00:02:24.607
If you actually want to do it,
you go head first but

00:02:24.607 --> 00:02:26.583
if there's a part of you that
likes the narrative that

00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:28.460
it paints on you 
as a human being

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.117
and you're concerned about 
the other parts like

00:02:30.117 --> 00:02:31.242
money and other things,

00:02:31.242 --> 00:02:34.376
you don't have to beat 
yourself up about that.

00:02:34.376 --> 00:02:36.312
(light music)

